description:
Design a 4-bit Johnson counter with support for asynchronous reset. The counter utilizes a 64-bit shift register to generate a sequence of output states, where the most significant four bits (Q) are provided as output. On a negative edge of the reset signal, the shift register and output are initialized to zero; otherwise, on each positive clock edge, the shift register is updated by shifting in a feedback signal derived from specific bits of the shift register, effectively implementing the Johnson counting sequence. The feedback logic utilizes a selection of shift register bits to create the required toggle behavior.
module top_module(
  input                clk,
  input                rst_n,
  output reg  [3:0]    Q
);

code:
module top_module(
  input                clk,
  input                rst_n,
  output reg  [3:0]    Q
);reg [63:0] shift_reg;
  reg [3:0] feedback;

  always @(posedge clk or negedge rst_n) begin
    if (~rst_n) begin
      shift_reg <= 64'b0;
      feedback <= 4'b0000;
      Q <= 4'b0000;
    end
    else begin
      shift_reg <= {shift_reg[62:0], feedback[3]};
      feedback <= {shift_reg[0], shift_reg[31], shift_reg[47], shift_reg[55]};
      Q <= shift_reg[63:60];
    end
  end

endmodule

