description:
Design a 4-bit Gray code state machine that incrementally generates the Gray code equivalent of a binary count. Upon a reset signal, the module initializes the binary counter and outputs the corresponding Gray code value. On each clock edge, it increments the binary value by one and computes the new Gray code using the formula `Gray = Binary ^ (Binary >> 1)`. The module captures the previous Gray code value but does not utilize it in current computations beyond tracking state.
module top_module(
  input clk,
  input rst,
  output reg gray
);

code:
module top_module(
  input clk,
  input rst,
  output reg gray
);reg [3:0] binary;
  reg [3:0] gray_prev;

  always @(posedge clk, posedge rst) begin
    if (rst) begin
      binary <= 4'b0000;
      gray_prev <= 4'b0000;
      gray <= 4'b0000;
    end
    else begin
      binary <= binary + 1;
      gray <= binary ^ (binary >> 1);
      gray_prev <= gray;
    end
  end

endmodule

