Design a combinational circuit that performs multiplication of two 4-bit unsigned integers (A and B) to produce an 8-bit product (P). The module utilizes bitwise AND operations followed by left-shifting and summation to compute the final product, effectively implementing the standard binary multiplication algorithm. Each bit of A is used to generate partial products with B, which are then aligned based on their respective bit positions before being summed together to yield the final result.
module top_module(
    input [3:0] A,
    input [3:0] B,
    output reg [7:0] P
);

